<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Chapter 30 — Distributed Transactions. FoodFleet order placement without 2PC:
    orders/    POST /orders writes the order (PENDING) and an outbox row in one local transaction; OrderRelay
               claims outbox rows and hands them to payments, then confirms or rejects the orders
    payments/  PaymentLedger applies a batch idempotently (debit rows keyed by order id), locks stock and
               wallets in key order, falls back to one-by-one so a single failure rejects a single order
    indoubt/   for systems that do use two-phase commit: find prepared transactions left in doubt and resolve
               them from the coordinator's decision log (presumed abort)
    verify/    the chapter's experiments on two PostgreSQL clusters (local vs 2PC vs saga vs outbox)
  The two schemas stand in for two services' databases: no transaction ever spans both.
-->
